700:`spec.k` is a set of K reachability claims. `kprove` attempts to prove each claim by symbolically executing from the LHS and checking it reaches the RHS under the given conditions. When the proof fails, `kprove` exits non-zero and prints a residual configuration — the state it reached but could not close. This skill provides the tools to read that residual and extend `verification.k` until the proof closes.
702:Use `writing-spec` before this skill if `spec.k` is not yet written.
