9735:The semantics deliberately keeps two branches for abstract function frames: plain locals versus closure-cell locals. A negative map-membership guard is not strong enough for its symbolic map solver to prune the cell branch. The real comprehension frame is exact: after the first iteration it has only `$acc`, `score`, and `predicted`. I’m anchoring the circularity there; the entry proof will execute the empty case or first iteration under fixed semantics before applying it.
